From b8eedbe79c63c268de65648bb0df2d5e94b35d56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 22:39:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00883/11171] [outer-loop] FIX root-cause of 97% truncation:
 wrong stop token (</s> vs <|im_end|>)

The instrumentation (operator-directed) caught base truncation_rate=0.967 -> TRUNCATION_
INVALID, preventing a FALSE positive (process_weighted 0.633 vs base 0.367 'teaches!' was
mostly training teaching the model to STOP, not reasoning). Root cause: the chat template
ends the turn with <|im_end|> (id 130073, which the model emits) but eval passed
eos_token_id=tok.eos_token_id=</s>(1) which the chat model NEVER emits -> generation never
stopped. generation_config lists both [1, 130073]. Fix: stop on BOTH. Re-running; the
truncation_rate will confirm base now stops (and whether the earlier 0.49 'headroom' holds).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
